    <x:String x:Key="Net_CauseWithUrl">{0} Address: {1}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Net_AfterFailureCause">Could not download {0}. {1}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Net_AfterFailureCauseHosts">Could not download {0}. {1} Not answering: {2}.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Net_CauseDns">The site's address was not found (DNS). Check the connection; if a VPN or a proxy is on, switch it over.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Net_CauseRefused">The connection was refused. If a proxy or a VPN is set in Windows, check that it is running.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Net_CauseReset">The connection was cut on the way. A provider's block or security software does this.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Net_CauseUnreachable">There is no route to the site. Check the internet connection.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Net_CauseCertificate">Windows does not trust the certificate the site showed. Usually an antivirus or a proxy is inspecting HTTPS: switch that inspection off there or add the launcher to its exceptions.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Net_CauseTls">A secure connection could not be set up. An antivirus, a proxy or the provider may be in the way.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Net_CauseTimeout">The site did not answer in time.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Net_CauseHttp">The site answered with an error: {0}.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Net_CauseHash">The file that came is not the one that was promised: the checksum does not match.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Net_CauseRedirect">The site sent the download to an address the launcher does not follow: {0}.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Mods_CatalogPinnedHint">The server catalog sets this mod's version - updates arrive with the build.</x:String>

    <!-- Backup restore -->
    <x:String x:Key="Settings_BackupsWhat">A backup holds worlds, mods, configs, resource packs, shaders, game options and the build definition, so both the worlds and the whole build can be restored from it.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Settings_BackupsList">Saved backups</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Backup_Restore">Restore</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Backup_RestoreWorlds">Worlds only</x:String>
