    <x:String x:Key="Host_JoinAskDetail">Minecraft {0} · {1}. If that is not the server's version, the game will not get in. Nothing is changed in the build.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_JoinAskAction">Start with it</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_JoinVersionUnknown">The launcher does not know this server's version, so it will not pick a build by itself. Select a build of the right version on the Builds tab and press the button again.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_JoinNoBuild">None of your builds fits this server (Minecraft {0} · {1}), and the launcher cannot make one right now. Make a build of this version on the Builds tab.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_InviteBuildExisting">Played with your build “{0}”</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_InviteBuildExistingDetail">Minecraft {0} · {1}: it fits this server. Nothing is created or downloaded, and the build is not changed.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_BuildBack">The server “{0}” has a build again: “{1}”. Press “Play”.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_AskingVersion">Asking the server which version it runs…</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_BuildGoneConfirm">The build for this server was deleted and none of yours fits it. Above is what would be made instead; nothing is made until you agree.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_VersionUnknown">The launcher does not know which version this server runs and will not guess a build for it. Ask your friend for a new invite.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Memory_ForNoMods">for the game without mods</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Memory_ForModsOne">for {0} mod</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Memory_ForModsMany">for {0} mods</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Memory_WithShaders">{0} and shaders</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Memory_MachineLimit">{0}; the build would take {1} MB, but this computer needs the rest</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_CopyInvite">Copy the invite</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_InviteTitle">HOW TO INVITE A FRIEND</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_Step1Done">The server is running</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_Step1DoneNote">It runs while the launcher is open.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_Step1Todo">Start the server</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_Step1TodoNote">The “Start” button is on the server's card above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_Step1WorkingNote">The server is starting or stopping; it does not take long.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_Step2">Put your friend's nickname on the list</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_Step2Note">The server lets in only the nicknames on the list. Spell it exactly as in your friend's launcher.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_Step3">Send your friend the code</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_Step3Note">Your friend pastes the code under “Friends”, on the “Join a friend” tab. The mods of your build are set up for them by the launcher. The code works while the server is running.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_InviteCopy">Copy</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_InvitePlaceholder">The code appears here once the server is running and you press “Copy”.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_InviteLongCopied">The long invite line is copied</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_OnlineLabel">ON THE SERVER NOW</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_OnlineTitle">On the server now</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_SettingsPort">Port</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_SettingsHint">Changed while the server is stopped; used from the next start.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_SettingsPortHint">The port matters for the “Directly” way. If another program holds it, the launcher offers a free one.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_FilesTitle">Folder and removal</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_FolderHint">The server's folder holds the world, the mods and the settings files.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_RemoveAsk">Take the server off the list? The folder with the world stays on the disk.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_OpenFolder">Open the server's folder</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_Remove">Take off the list</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_RemoveHint">The server leaves the launcher, but nothing is deleted: its folder, world included, moves to servers/.removed. A running server cannot be taken off.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_PortChip">port {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_MemoryChip">{0} of memory</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_BasedOn">from the build “{0}”</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_BasedOnGone">the build it was made from is gone</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_PlayersOffline">Players show up here once the server is running</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_PlayersNone">Nobody is on the server yet</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_PlayersCount">On the server: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_Console">Server console</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_ConsoleEmpty">The server's output shows up here once it starts</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_CommandHint">A command for the server, for example: say Hello</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_Send">Send the command</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_CommandNoServer">The server is not running - there is nobody to carry the command out</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_Whitelist">Who may join</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WhitelistHint">Only players on this list can join. A nickname is written exactly as in the friend's launcher: capital and small letters differ. A nickname is not a password: the server lets in whoever joins under a listed one, so give the address only to people you trust.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WhitelistAdd">A friend's nickname</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WhitelistAddButton">Add</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WhitelistRemoveTip">Take off the list</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WhitelistExists">{0} is already on the list</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WhitelistAdded">{0} can now join the server</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WhitelistRemoved">{0} can no longer join the server</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_ModsSoon">The server's mods will be here. For now they can be put into the server's mods folder by hand: the folder button on the server's card.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_OtherRunning">Stop the server “{0}” first: one runs at a time.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_NoticePort">Port {0} is taken by another program - perhaps another Minecraft server is already running.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_UseFreePort">Take a free port</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_PortChanged">The server's port is now {0}. Press “Start”.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_NoticeJavaMissing">The server needs Java {0} and this computer has none. The download site does not answer right now - check the connection and try again.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_NoticeJavaPath">Java was not where the search found it. Try again.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_NoticeJavaDownload">Java could not be downloaded: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_NoticeLaunch">The server could not be started: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_NoticeDownload">The server could not be downloaded: {0}. Check the connection and press “Start” again.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_NoticeKilled">The server did not stop in time and was closed by force. The last minutes of play may not have been saved.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_NoticeEula">The server did not start: eula.txt does not agree to the licence.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_NoticeWrongJava">The server did not start: it needs a newer Java than the one it was started with.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_NoticeMemory">Java could not get {0} of memory. Lower the memory on the “Server settings” tab and start again.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_NoticeWorldInUse">The server's world is open in another program - perhaps another server or the game.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_NoticeFailedToStart">The server could not start (code {0}). The last lines of the console say why.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_NoticeCrash">The server went down with an error (code {0}). The console below shows what happened.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_Starting">The server is starting: the world is loading…</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_Ready">The server “{0}” is running. Friends can be invited now.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_Stopping">Stopping the server, the world is being saved…</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_Stopped">The server is stopped, the world is saved</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_ConsentInstallTitle">The server has not been downloaded yet</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_ConsentInstallAction">Download</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_ConsentJavaTitle">The server needs Java {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_ConsentJavaAction">Download Java and start</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_ConsentEulaTitle">The Minecraft licence agreement</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_ConsentEulaLine">A Minecraft server only starts once Mojang's agreement (EULA) is accepted</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_ConsentEulaDetail">By pressing the button you confirm that you have read it and accept it.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_ConsentEulaAction">I accept, start</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WaysTitle">WAYS OF CONNECTING</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WaysHint">Switch on one way or several. The invite carries what is on and already working.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WayOff">Off</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WayPending">Comes on when the server is running</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WayRelay">Friends only</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WayRelayText">Friends with STlauncher join by the invite. Nothing to set up: the connection goes through a relay server, no ports to open.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_RelayNotConfigured">The relay server is not set up yet, so this way is not available. The other two work without it.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_RelayWorking">Connecting to the relay {0}…</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_RelayReady">Ready: friends join by the invite</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_RelayUnreachable">The relay {0} does not answer. The launcher keeps trying.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_RelayBusy">The relay is at its limit right now. The launcher keeps trying.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_RelayRejected">The relay refused the connection: the launcher may need an update.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WayDirect">Directly</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WayDirectWarning">Open ports are required. This works only when your provider gives you a public IP address and the router has UPnP on, or port {0} is forwarded by hand. Otherwise friends will not get through: use the invite way.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WayDirectText">Friends connect straight to your computer. The launcher asks the router to open port {0} and checks from outside that the server can be reached. The port closes together with the server.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_DirectWorking">Talking to the router and checking from outside…</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_DirectReady">Ready, checked from outside</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_DirectReadyUnverified">The port is open. There is nothing to check it from outside with: no relay is set up</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_DirectNoGateway">The router did not answer: UPnP is switched off in it, or it has none. Switch UPnP on in the router's settings, or pick another way.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_DirectRefused">The router refused to open the port.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_DirectBehindNat">Your provider keeps the router behind a shared address, so a direct connection cannot work: use the invite way.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_DirectNotReachable">The router opened the port, yet the server cannot be reached from outside: the provider or the Windows firewall is in the way.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_DirectError">The router stopped answering. Switch the way off and on again.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_VoiceRelay">Voice chat: friends who join by the invite hear each other</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_VoiceDirectWorking">Voice chat: asking the router to open UDP port {0}…</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_VoiceDirectReady">Voice chat: the router opened UDP port {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_VoiceDirectFailed">Voice chat: the router did not open UDP port {0}, so friends who connect directly will not hear each other</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_InviteNeedsServer">Start the server first: the invite is put together while it runs.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_InviteNeedsWay">Switch on at least one way of connecting and wait until it is ready.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_InviteBusy">Putting the invite together…</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_InviteCopiedShort">The invite is copied: {0}. Send it to a friend: they paste the code under “Friends”, on the “Join a friend” tab. The code works while your server is running. Remember to put their nickname on the list.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_ShortNoRelay">This is a short invite, and the launcher does not know the server that keeps such invites yet. Ask the friend for the long one, or try again later.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_ShortFetching">Asking for the invite {0}…</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_ShortUnreachable">The server that keeps invites does not answer. Check the connection and try again.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_ShortOffline">Nobody answers to the invite {0}: the friend's server is not running right now, or the code has a typo.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_InviteCopied">The invite is copied. Send it to a friend: they paste the line under “Friends”, on the “Join a friend” tab. Remember to put their nickname on the list.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_InviteCopiedMissing">The invite is copied. These mods are not on Modrinth and have to be handed over separately: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_InviteCopiedNoBuild">The invite is copied without the build: Modrinth did not answer. The friend will need a build of their own for {0}.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_InviteFailed">The invite could not be put together: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_Removed">The server “{0}” is off the list. Its folder with the world is intact: {1}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_RemoveFailed">Could not take the server off the list: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_SaveFailed">Could not save the server's settings: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_LoadFailed">Could not read the list of servers: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_Unreadable">A server could not be read and was left untouched: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_CloseTitle">The server is still running</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_CloseText">The server “{0}” is running. Closing the launcher stops it: the world is saved, the players are disconnected and the addresses opened for friends are closed.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_CloseConfirm">Stop and close</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_CloseConfirmUpdate">Stop and update</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_CloseTunnelTitle">You are on a friend's server</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_CloseTextTunnel">The game is connected to the friend's server through the launcher. Closing the launcher breaks that connection.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_CloseConfirmTunnel">Close anyway</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_CloseCancel">Keep it open</x:String>

    <!-- My server: the server's mods and their settings -->
    <x:String x:Key="HostMods_Installed">On the server · {0}</x:String>
